  "description": "Reusable .NET 10 package that wraps ASP.NET Core Identity with cookie and JWT auth, Google OAuth, a pluggable e-mail provider, a multi-tenant model with dynamic RBAC (roles + module permissions), and secure defaults — wired up with a single AddMyIdentity call. JWT and Google OAuth secrets are supplied by the consumer (never shipped in the package).",
  "id": "MyIdentity",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-30T00:34:56.283Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "ViCgJQjMxtyReST44nQFoEuWnQAz/hBBOO0FvhhQ0AB8CQe37cpNSkRirFVV0KINo/6QukB29BjV5JRohIcidg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 664157,
  "published": "2026-10-30T00:30:14.153Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.0: a read-only door to who holds which role, and the last library text no describer reached. New opt-in MyIdentityPermissionOptions.AllowDelegatedRoleAssignmentRead (default false, code-only): with it on, a caller granted Read on IdentityModuleCode tenant-wide reads their own tenant's user-role assignments (GetUserRoleAssignmentsAsync, GetUserRoleAssignmentsForUserAsync, GetUserRoleAssignmentAsync), confined as a TenantAdmin is; no write, no security events. Modify implies Read, so audit the grants on your identity module before turning it on. New MyIdentityMessageDescriber.SystemAdminAlreadyExists() and MyIdentityErrorCodes.SystemAdminAlreadyExists: the first-run refusal takes its text from the describer, with the same code. Nothing breaks at the signature level; a describer of your own has one new method to translate. The package validation baseline is 5.7.0. Upgrading from 5.7.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §52.",
